00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:03.170
But I'm going to look it up.

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:05.690
I think it's Falling Down.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.510
Falling Down is the movie.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:12.550
And the reason why I bring that up in this particular episode is because that's how I feel like Dr.

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.330
Jekyll's day is going, you know?

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.950
Like, it's such a great day for him.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.590
He's about to get married and everything.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:23.450
But the actual game, everyone and everything is working against you.

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.310
There's never a good moment.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:37.450
And I'm surprised that there's no, like, Castlevania II element to this where you can, like, talk to townspeople and they can be, like, you know, give some world building and be like, yeah, I don't know what's going on.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.650
Like, what's in the air today?

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:45.970
Or, like, you know, it just seems strange that everyone in this game says, I'm going to, you know, like, F up this guy's shit today.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:56.810
Like, I'm really going to mess with him, you know, knowing that he's, like, fully dressed in a, you know, in a nice suit and everything and birds are pooping on him and he's getting bombs dropped on him.

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.370
The bombs! It's crazy, guys.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:07.470
Yeah, like, the Jekyll parts of this game feel like, to me, what really entitled people must, like, like, how they describe their day.

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:13.130
Like, oh, everybody was out to get me and nothing could possibly go right.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.850
It's like this finally coming to fruition.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:19.210
That's sort of how I was interpreting it.

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:23.930
I bet a lot of those people played this game as kids and that's why they're like that now.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:31.230
Yeah, it even gets to the point where, like, it looks, I thought I was, like, far in the game, but I'm, like, watching a video of it now.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:34.330
I think I was, like, not even halfway through or maybe a little bit over halfway through.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.910
But it's, like, the third or fourth screen.

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:40.010
It just, people just compound on you.

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:41.650
Like, there's just no...

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:42.890
There's no way out.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:45.150
There's no gaps between the people.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:48.550
Not even the other, not even the dogs or the bombs or the birds or whatever.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:49.390
Just people.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.150
Just charging from left and right.

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:52.950
Just haul all over the place. There's nothing you can do.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:54.470
It's kind of absurd.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.770
And that's what I really think happens here.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:03.630
I mean, I know we're not getting, like, too deep into gameplay or anything, but it's because I'm still shocked by the absurdity of the game.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:10.370
Like, the fact that you could have bought this and plugged this into your NES and played it.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:13.770
And I don't think anybody was guessing this is what a Dr.

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.850
Jackal and Mr. Hyde game was going to be.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:20.530
Am I wrong? Like, did you guys actually think this was going to be the game?

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:22.110
No, not at all.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:24.370
But I'll say that it...

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:28.130
I feel like I say this about a lot of games that I don't like.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:32.150
But, like, it's an interesting way to make a Dr.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.270
Jekyll and Mr. Hyde game where Mr.

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:37.070
Hyde has a different sort of goal, quote unquote.

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:40.370
Or is, like, is undoing progress or is hurting your progress.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:41.370
Like, that...

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:49.730
In theory, that makes sense that you would want for a game like this where it's about, like, the dichotomy of your two personalities to have something like that.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.710
It's just... It just doesn't work.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:56.630
Yeah, like, I think back to Vampire the Masquerade.

00:18:56.850 --> 00:19:03.010
Like, if you don't get enough blood or something along those lines, you'll go into a frenzy.

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:09.590
And, like, a whole thing about the game is you're trying to uphold the masquerade and, like, not let people know that vampires exist.

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:15.650
And when you frenzy, like, you lose all input and you go mess up people's day and murder people.

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:18.470
And, like, it's supposed to be, like, a thing you don't want to happen.

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:26.010
But that sort of, like, counters itself because there's a lot of other things going on in the game.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.850
Whereas this is...

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:34.230
Like, it's definitely a huge part of the game.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:39.210
But the gameplay loop is just so ludicrous.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:41.970
It's hard to get on board.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:44.850
Yeah, and I think I understand what you're saying, Joe.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.630
Like, there's no doubt this is an interesting game.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:51.250
Like, we haven't played one like this.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:59.090
And, you know, a lot of times we say, like, you know, well, if they fix some of the execution, like, maybe it would be a great game.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.370
I don't know here.

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:01.770
I don't know if this is... It's just...

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:04.030
There's so much going against it.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:08.850
In terms of, like, the frustrating amounts of things that happened to you.

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:13.990
And, you know, just being in Jekyll's London.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:17.970
Like, just that experience is just not very fun.

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:23.550
And it's so, like, not of the times.

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:37.410
Like, when I look at the games that we've been playing in 1989 and before that, this just doesn't come off as, like, something kids would want to play and something that would be fun.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:40.190
Like, it just feels like it's completely in the wrong market.

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.630
It just feels like such an oddity.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.610
And so I appreciate all that stuff.

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:46.270
Like, it's weird what they...

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:49.870
You know, like, oh, this could be a way to make, like, an incredible Hulk game.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.150
If that makes sense.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.730
You know? Like, take the same exact game.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:55.150
Why did you choose Dr.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:59.570
Jekyll and Mr. Hyde? Like, this could have been a great game where, like, you're Bruce Banner doing...

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:00.410
Trying to, like, solve...

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:07.450
But that also sounds like not a way that you would make a Hulk game where you want to be Banner the whole time.

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:08.890
Well, right. That would be Omegon.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:12.190
Right, right. Right. An incredible Hulk game would be like Omegon from last week.

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:13.270
I hear you. Yeah.

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:15.750
I don't know what the solution is here.

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:18.590
They did lay down, like, an interesting idea for a game.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:20.130
I'm just not... I'm not down with it.

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:23.870
It's kind of like that time that Ghostbusters was turned into, like, a...

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:24.930
An economic simulator?

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:29.450
Yeah, you're part of the Ghostbusters franchise and you've got to manage your money and stuff.

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:30.610
Like, that was bizarre.

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:32.710
So, that's what this is.

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:34.090
It's just a very bizarre game.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:36.430
I don't really know how to judge it.

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:40.910
Well, before we judge it, we have to take everything into account.

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:44.150
We never mentioned the bribery system.

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:45.590
Would you like to talk about it?

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:56.630
Yeah. I never really fully understood how it worked, but apparently you can pay people to stop being assholes with money that you find as Mr.

00:21:56.730 --> 00:22:02.810
Hyde, which I imagine, like, in the real world, you're actually just mugging these people for their money.

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:06.590
And that's sort of...

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:07.870
And then giving it back to them, though?

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:11.450
Like, giving it back to them to make them stop singing so terribly.

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:17.330
But I just wanted to make sure that we at least touched upon that before we fully...

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:18.230
Oh, I wasn't...

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:21.690
Yeah, I wasn't jumping to the Essential Games list yet because I also wanted to talk about the cane.

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.970
Does that really do anything?

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:25.510
I couldn't find a use for it.

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:28.690
Yeah, I assume that you have to hit someone a million times.

00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:30.750
More than 16 times, like last week.

00:22:31.370 --> 00:22:34.710
16. To kill anyone because I never killed anything with that cane.

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:37.250
And so that's like another part of the absurdity, though, right?

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:38.170
Like, you get...

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:42.010
The button does something and it doesn't seem like it's doing anything.

00:22:42.450 --> 00:22:43.770
Yeah. Well, even...

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:49.970
The only time that I could interact with an obstacle or enemy was when I ate the fly or the bee.

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:52.170
Like, that's the only thing that I could do.

00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:53.350
You ate it?

00:22:53.650 --> 00:22:56.410
It sounds like that was just like a glitch in your game.

00:22:56.670 --> 00:23:04.430
Every single time I crouched in front of a bug, it, like, gave me a little boop and then it went away.

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:06.050
Wow. I missed that.

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:08.070
But I don't know what that was about.

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:11.650
But that was the only way to interact with any of these enemies.

00:23:12.270 --> 00:23:13.330
Yeah. Well, even when you're Mr.

00:23:13.430 --> 00:23:16.710
Hyde and you interact, you have, like, a fire flower type thing.

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:21.850
But instead of, like, bouncing off the ground, it, like, sometimes it'll go below the hitbox of the ground.

00:23:22.010 --> 00:23:23.030
Oh, that's good. Psycho.

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:28.230
And, like, dips down and then it, like, comes back up around and, like, hits things from behind or something.

00:23:28.230 --> 00:23:30.890
But you have no control over it, so you only hit things, like, once in a while.

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:33.070
Or if they're, like, directly in front of you.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:35.010
Yeah. Like, it didn't even do the, like...

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:35.950
Yeah, the path is wild.

00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:37.630
Yeah, yeah.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:41.910
It didn't even do the, like, you feel so overpowered as Mr.

00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:45.850
Hyde or anything because you actually feel, you know, a little more useful.

00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:48.290
But you still feel kind of helpless compared to most games.

00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:51.970
So is the reputation of this game fair?

00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:58.970
You know, I looked to, again, the angry video game nerd who did, like, I think this was his second episode.

00:24:00.590 --> 00:24:06.390
And, you know, I think it's a 48-second video where he just shows how quickly you can die in the game.

00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:16.550
And a lot of people have just said, like, you know, oh, now that I've seen that video or now that I played it afterwards, like, this is one of the worst games of all time.

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:21.810
And there's even an entry for it in a Wikipedia article on list of worst games of all time.

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:24.230
So is that fair?

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:26.110
Did it earn that?

00:24:26.270 --> 00:24:27.870
Is that exaggerated a bit?

00:24:28.050 --> 00:24:32.210
What do you think, Joe? I think it depends on how big your list is.

00:24:32.430 --> 00:24:37.790
Definitely think that we've played plenty of games that are worse than this just on the NES alone.

00:24:38.310 --> 00:24:47.450
So if I were to put this in, like, if it was just, like, chunks of, like, of, like, how, you know, if we were rating it out of 10, this would definitely be down there with the ones and zeros for me.

00:24:47.570 --> 00:24:52.590
But if I were actually ranking them on, like, a spectrum, I think there's plenty that are worse than this game.

00:24:52.590 --> 00:24:57.530
I'd say that I'd keep this, like, in that list of worst games of all time.

00:24:57.770 --> 00:25:03.230
But that video does overstate how bad it is.

00:25:03.350 --> 00:25:08.170
Like, I guess, like, one of the worst games of all time that has a reputation.

00:25:08.530 --> 00:25:11.990
Because, yeah, there are a ton of terrible games.

00:25:12.010 --> 00:25:14.490
And this one's almost unplayable.

00:25:14.630 --> 00:25:19.890
But at least it's one of those so bad that it's interesting.

00:25:19.890 --> 00:25:22.790
Not so bad that it's good, but so bad that it's interesting.

00:25:23.290 --> 00:25:26.990
Because it has such a weird and wacky way of going about its terribleness.

00:25:28.590 --> 00:25:32.210
So, yeah, a little exaggerated in that video, but still plenty bad.

00:25:32.790 --> 00:25:34.670
Yeah, I think that's how I feel, too, Sean.

00:25:34.830 --> 00:25:38.830
Is, like, you know, so bad that it actually makes it interesting.

00:25:39.090 --> 00:25:46.830
Because the real, like, 99% of the actual bad games that have ever been created are, like, flash games that nobody remembers anymore.

00:25:46.830 --> 00:25:49.550
You know, like, do those even count?

00:25:49.710 --> 00:25:50.590
Like, probably not.

00:25:50.690 --> 00:25:53.250
You should probably only count official releases and stuff like that.

00:25:53.330 --> 00:25:54.290
But even then, still.

00:25:54.650 --> 00:26:01.650
Like, there are games that are just, like, the game is Super Mario Brothers, but we made it worse in every way possible.

00:26:01.650 --> 00:26:03.810
Right? And those are, like, the actual bad games.

00:26:04.050 --> 00:26:05.050
Like the shovelware. Yeah.

00:26:05.210 --> 00:26:07.650
Right. They didn't do anything to change it.

00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:10.590
And they actually made it worse than the games they were trying to rip off.

00:26:11.150 --> 00:26:19.590
This is at least, as we've been saying, it's absurd enough for me to say, like, I'm not upset that I spent some time playing this game.

00:26:19.830 --> 00:26:25.410
Like, it was an interesting experience to include this in the list of video games I've ever played.

00:26:26.150 --> 00:26:33.330
Absolutely. Sean, you were asking about the ending for the game, if he gets married or not.

00:26:33.330 --> 00:26:34.650
There are two endings.

00:26:35.170 --> 00:26:37.870
So, if you get to the church as Dr.

00:26:38.070 --> 00:26:42.250
Jekyll, then you have gotten the bad ending, believe it or not.

00:26:42.490 --> 00:26:43.390
Oh, okay. Yeah.

00:26:43.950 --> 00:26:47.130
That's the bad ending because you just, you made the game too easy.

00:26:47.610 --> 00:26:51.010
And, therefore, when you get to the church, you just see the end.

00:26:51.290 --> 00:26:52.130
And that's it.

00:26:52.270 --> 00:26:53.870
No cut scene or anything.

00:26:53.870 --> 00:26:55.670
You don't get to see if the wedding happened or not.

00:26:55.670 --> 00:26:58.630
You just get the end and you have to reset your NES.

00:26:59.570 --> 00:27:11.570
Wow. However, if you can get to the church or close enough to the church and then get your stress meter built up before getting to the end, that will allow you to transform into Mr.

00:27:11.730 --> 00:27:22.390
Hyde. And this is the only level, because it's the final level, where you won't have to worry about, you know, reaching the same point as where you were with Dr.

00:27:22.430 --> 00:27:26.350
Jekyll because now the bolt of lightning that kills you is no longer there.

00:27:26.350 --> 00:27:33.590
And so when you get to the church, there's a big boss fight with, like, a floating head.

00:27:33.670 --> 00:27:38.290
And I can't really tell what that floating head is supposed to represent, but it's like a demon.

00:27:38.450 --> 00:27:40.750
So I guess that's the whole, like, demon world thing.

00:27:40.750 --> 00:27:45.530
But it takes so many shots of your psycho wave to kill this thing.

00:27:45.710 --> 00:27:55.430
And like Joe was mentioning, because of the unpredictability of that psycho wave and the fact that the floating head, like, vanishes from screen and reappears.

00:27:55.430 --> 00:27:58.470
Even some of, like, the fastest YouTube videos I've seen.

00:27:58.650 --> 00:28:01.530
It takes these guys a while to kill the floating head.

00:28:01.850 --> 00:28:08.510
But if you manage to do that, you will actually get to see the marriage of Dr.

00:28:08.650 --> 00:28:10.470
Jekyll and Miss Millicent.

00:28:10.610 --> 00:28:13.450
So at least you get that.

00:28:13.510 --> 00:28:21.810
I think it is a little strange, though, that you have to, like, fill up your stress meter on the final level like you were supposed to know that.

00:28:21.810 --> 00:28:25.010
So you can't win this game?

00:28:25.170 --> 00:28:31.790
Like, you can't go and actually, like, get to the church not being Mr.

00:28:31.870 --> 00:28:33.290
Hyde? You have to be Mr.

00:28:33.410 --> 00:28:38.070
Hyde to get the cutscene because, Sean, you have to face your demons.

00:28:38.570 --> 00:28:40.070
Oh, yes, I see.

00:28:40.470 --> 00:28:42.250
Everybody has to do that before they get married.

00:28:42.250 --> 00:28:43.790
It's like part of the counseling stage.

00:28:43.810 --> 00:28:44.830
You have to face your demons.

00:28:45.990 --> 00:28:47.410
Joe, any thoughts on the ending?

00:28:48.290 --> 00:28:51.790
I mean, it's, again, it's, like, interesting and unique.

00:28:51.790 --> 00:28:56.310
I don't think it's necessarily something that makes a good video game.

00:28:56.430 --> 00:28:58.110
I think, yeah, I think they were just off the mark.

00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:05.590
In the sequels and spinoffs section here, the only thing I have is a video game from 2001 called Jekyll and Hyde.

00:29:05.910 --> 00:29:07.790
It was only available on Windows.

00:29:08.950 --> 00:29:14.490
And the only thing to note here is that on Wikipedia, they don't really tell you what the game is or anything like that.

00:29:14.490 --> 00:29:17.090
But they say it was praised for its sound effects.

00:29:17.350 --> 00:29:18.450
And I thought that was funny.

00:29:19.450 --> 00:29:22.610
It's like they're looking for something to praise them about.

00:29:23.230 --> 00:29:24.910
Yeah, yeah, exactly. Like, but who?

00:29:25.290 --> 00:29:26.350
Like, was it anyone notable?

00:29:26.690 --> 00:29:27.810
What sound effect? Like, what?

00:29:28.290 --> 00:29:29.570
Everything's a beep and a boop.

00:29:29.850 --> 00:29:30.710
I mean, when was this?

00:29:30.810 --> 00:29:32.510
What year was this? 2001.

00:29:32.990 --> 00:29:35.090
So, you know, not beeps and boops anymore.

00:29:35.110 --> 00:29:37.490
Oh, I'm sorry. I completely blanked.

00:29:38.370 --> 00:29:40.330
I was like, this game that we've just played?

00:29:40.750 --> 00:29:41.750
No, no, yeah, yeah.

00:29:41.750 --> 00:29:47.810
I thought maybe if it was a little earlier, if it was like right around the time that, you know, I don't even know what year it would be.

00:29:47.930 --> 00:29:56.270
But when we're hearing sound effects that are like that weird muffled, like it's like an actual recording, but it's like really compressed.

00:29:56.550 --> 00:30:00.550
And then maybe these people figured out how to like make it sound nicer or something.

00:30:00.730 --> 00:30:04.630
But 2001, I mean, at that point, it's just sounds.

00:30:04.630 --> 00:30:08.750
And I think it's also worth remembering that Dr.

00:30:08.990 --> 00:30:14.190
Jekyll was a pretty important character in the Dark Universe.

00:30:14.630 --> 00:30:21.890
The failed Universal Studios, you know, the mummy, Dracula, Dr.

00:30:22.030 --> 00:30:24.470
Jekyll. Russell Crowe was playing Dr.

00:30:24.630 --> 00:30:29.670
Jekyll in the mummy movie with Tom Cruise.

00:30:29.670 --> 00:30:31.770
Well, who played Dr.

00:30:31.910 --> 00:30:33.530
Jekyll in the League of Extraordinary Gentlemen?

00:30:34.090 --> 00:30:35.550
Oh, that's a good question.

00:30:36.650 --> 00:30:40.830
Hmm. Not showing up right here, but let's get an answer because why not?

00:30:40.910 --> 00:30:41.730
That would be more interesting.

00:30:41.950 --> 00:30:44.610
Although Russell Crowe probably could have done a good job for what it's worth.

00:30:45.330 --> 00:30:46.770
I think so.

00:30:47.830 --> 00:30:48.830
Jason Fleming.

00:30:49.530 --> 00:30:50.730
Sorry. There you go.

00:30:50.990 --> 00:30:53.470
